<title>TURKEY: Turk Sise Cam 96 net profit up 138.4 pct.</title>
<headline>Turk Sise Cam 96 net profit up 138.4 pct.</headline>
<dateline>ISTANBUL 1997-03-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>1996 final results</p>
<p>(billion lira unless stated)</p>
<p>    Per share profit (lira)     558.96  vs    570.86</p>
<p>    Net profit		    3,130.15  vs  1,312.99</p>
<p>    Net sales		     1,042.76  vs    565.98</p>
<p>    Operating loss		  101.09  vs	6.57 profit</p>
<p>    Exceptional income	  3,637.83  vs  1,676.92</p>
<p>    Exceptional expense	    15.67  vs	1.94</p>
<p>    Interest Paid		    35.63  vs    117.66</p>
<p>    Total debts		   1,028.47  vs  1,086.66</p>
<p>    Equity			 13,971.22  vs  5,953.36</p>
<p>    Capital			 5,600.00  vs  2,300.00</p>
<p>NOTE - Turkiye Sise Cam Fabrikalari A.S., owned 74.91 percent by T.Is Bankasi A.S., is the parent company of Turkey's biggest glass and glassware producing and marketing group.</p>
<p>The company plans to pay 500 lira dividend in the form of bonus shares per 1,000 lira nominal valued share from its 1996 profits after approval at the annual meeting of shareholders and directors on March 21.</p>
<p>The figures above do not take into account Turkey's 84.9 percent wholesale inflation in 1996.</p>
<p>-- Istanbul Newsroom +90-212-2750875</p>
</text>
